<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
  <!--
    GMLTopology.mml
    Runtime GML topology file registry and graph-law contracts.

    Content dictionary: urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1
    Source directory:   data/*.gml
    Runtime consumer:   FieldDag::load_gml() → src/world/gml_parser.cpp

    AUTHORITY BOUNDARY: GML files are topology inputs for geometry and legal-adjacency.
    They are not semantic authority. FieldDag::load_gml() creates TensorSubstrate
    descriptors from provider_id attributes; it does not create MicronautEntry objects.
    Only TrackLoader (JSON track files) and Factory::propose_create() may create
    MicronautEntry objects. Geometry-source provider_id → projection-only substrate.

    Two edge types:
      @semantic_step — Hamming-1 bit flip, weight=1.0 (horizontal movement)
      @phase_step    — C6 adjacent phase, weight=0.5 (vertical movement)
      @related_to    — topology adjacency, weight=1.0
      @fold_step     — complement fold edge, weight=1.0
      @delegates_to / @requires / @verifies / @produces / @part_of / @defines / @exposes
                     — semantic verb edges (metric_graph.gml, field graphs)

    File inventory (13 files):
      Topology graphs:
        unfold-graph.gml          — G_runtime = Q_3 □ C_6 (48 nodes, 120 edges)
        khanary_topology.gml      — semantic track Q3 + Q4 allocation slots (10 nodes)
        hypercube_Q3.gml          — pure Q3 (8 nodes, 16 edges incl. fold edges)
        hypercube_Q4.gml          — pure Q4 (16 nodes, 32 edges)
        ccc_n3.gml                — CCC_3 (24 nodes, 36 edges)
        ccc_n4.gml                — CCC_4 (64 nodes, 96 edges)
      Field graphs (geometry/projection only):
        metric_graph.gml          — METRIC-µ provider topology (18 nodes)
        quantum_field_boundaries.gml  — wave/boundary graph (3 nodes)
        tensor_field.gml          — TENSOR-µ bundle projection (2 nodes)
        entropy_gradient_field.gml    — entropy gating manifold (2 nodes)
        euclidean_gradient_field.gml  — conservative gradient field (2 nodes)
      Behavioral affinity graph (style hints only; not FoldGraph B topology):
        daemon_behavior_modes.gml    — optional mode-pair affinities/transitions
      Test fixture:
        sample.gml                — GML parser test fixture (3 nodes, 3 edges)
  -->

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>G_runtime</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msup>
      <mo>&#x25A1;</mo>
      <msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">ProductGraphLaw</csymbol>
        <ci>unfold-graph.gml</ci>
        <apply>
          <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">HypercubeQ</csymbol>
          <ci>n</ci>
        </apply>
        <apply>
          <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">PhaseCycleC6</csymbol>
        </apply>
        <cn>48</cn><!-- |V| = 2^n · 6 = 8 · 6 for n=3 -->
        <cn>120</cn><!-- |E| = 72 semantic + 48 phase -->
        <cn>5</cn><!-- deg(v) = n + 2 = 3 + 2 -->
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
ProductGraphLaw: G_runtime = Q_n □ C_6
  unfold-graph.gml implements this for n=3.
  |V| = 2^n · 6 = 48   (8 semantic addresses × 6 phases)
  |E| = n · 2^n · 6 + 6 · 2^n = 3·8·6 + 6·8 = 144+48 = 192  (corrected: semantic edges are undirected pairs)
  Semantic edge (b,θ) ↔ (b⊕eᵢ,θ): weight=1.0, verb="@semantic_step", Hamming distance 1
  Phase edge   (b,θ) ↔ (b,θ±1): weight=0.5, verb="@phase_step", C6 adjacent
  Legal atomic transition ↔ Hamming distance 1 in semantic dimension OR ±1 step in phase dimension.
  Vertex id encoding: id = b·6 + theta_idx, where b = b0 + 2·b1 + 4·b2.
  Semantic addresses (Q3): 000→REASON-µ, 001→CREATE-µ, 010→INFER-µ, 011→ELIZA,
                            100→TOOL-µ, 101→ORCH-µ, 110→MEM-µ, 111→Coordinator.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>SemanticBits</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub>
      <mo>&#x2208;</mo>
      <mo>&#x7B;</mo><mi>analysis</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>generation</mi><mo>&#x7D;</mo>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub>
      <mo>&#x2208;</mo>
      <mo>&#x7B;</mo><mi>active</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>memory-grounded</mi><mo>&#x7D;</mo>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub>
      <mo>&#x2208;</mo>
      <mo>&#x7B;</mo><mi>object-level</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>meta-orchestration</mi><mo>&#x7D;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">SemanticAddressSchema</csymbol>
        <ci>khanary_topology.gml</ci>
        <ci>hypercube_Q3.gml</ci>
        <list>
          <ci>b0_analysis_generation</ci>
          <ci>b1_active_memory</ci>
          <ci>b2_object_meta</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
SemanticAddressSchema: three semantic bits, each an orthogonal capability axis.
  b0: analysis(0) / generation(1)   — does the track consume or produce?
  b1: active(0)   / memory-grounded(1) — does it operate on live context or stored gram?
  b2: object(0)   / meta-orchestration(1) — does it work on domain objects or the runtime itself?
khanary_topology.gml: 8 Q3 nodes with track labels + 2 Q4 structural nodes (MORPHISM-µ, FIXED-POINT-µ).
hypercube_Q3.gml: 8 nodes with bit labels (000-111), 12 semantic edges + 4 fold edges (complement b→b̄).
  Fold edges connect complements: 000↔111, 001↔110, 010↔101, 011↔100. FQ3 is 4-regular, diameter 2.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>AllocationSlot</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mn>1</mn>
      <mo>&#x21D2;</mo>
      <mi>ALLOCATION</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">AllocationSlotLaw</csymbol>
        <ci>hypercube_Q4.gml</ci>
        <ci>khanary_topology.gml</ci>
        <list>
          <cn>0001</cn><!-- MORPHISM-µ -->
          <cn>0011</cn><!-- FIXED-POINT-µ -->
          <cn>1111</cn><!-- Coordinator counterpart -->
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
AllocationSlotLaw: Q4 extends Q3 by a fourth bit b3.
  b3=0: occupied Q3 micronauts (REASON-µ through Coordinator).
  b3=1: ALLOCATION slots — typed structural positions the Factory may mint new micronauts into.
  Canonical Q4 latent addresses (from GLOSSARY.md and khanary_topology.gml):
    (0,0,0,1) = MORPHISM-µ  — structural category morphism specialist
    (0,0,1,1) = FIXED-POINT-µ — fixed-point / convergence specialist
    (1,1,1,1) = Coordinator counterpart (dual)
  An unoccupied slot is not an error — it is a named address awaiting Factory minting.
  Factory::propose_create() uses these addresses for principled MicronautEntry creation.
  hypercube_Q4.gml is the pure 16-vertex Q4 topology (no track labels, geometry only).
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>CCC</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>V</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mrow>
        <mo>&#x7B;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo>
        <mo>|</mo>
        <mn>0</mn><mo>&#x2264;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mn>0</mn><mo>&#x2264;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi>
        <mo>&#x7D;</mo>
      </mrow>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">CubeConnectedCycles</csymbol>
        <ci>ccc_n3.gml</ci>
        <ci>ccc_n4.gml</ci>
        <list>
          <cn>3</cn><cn>24</cn><cn>36</cn><!-- n, |V|, |E| for CCC_3 -->
          <cn>4</cn><cn>64</cn><cn>96</cn><!-- n, |V|, |E| for CCC_4 -->
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
CubeConnectedCycles: CCC(n) is a 3-regular interconnection network.
  V = {(x,y) | 0 ≤ x &lt; 2^n, 0 ≤ y &lt; n}: 2^n · n vertices.
  Edges per vertex (x,y): cycle (x,(y+1) mod n), cycle (x,(y-1) mod n), XOR (x⊕2^y, y).
  CCC_3: 24 nodes, 36 edges.  CCC_4: 64 nodes, 96 edges.
  Role: parallel routing substrate. 3-regularity means constant router fan-out.
  XOR edges are the cross-cluster links (bit-flip across clusters at depth y).
  Cycle edges are the intra-cluster rotation links.
  Both files are geometry-only topology descriptions loaded by FieldDag::load_gml().
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>GravityScore</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mfrac>
        <mi>established_nodes</mi>
        <msup><mi>distance</mi><mn>2</mn></msup>
      </mfrac>
      <mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">GravityWellGeometry</csymbol>
        <list>
          <ci>unfold-graph.gml</ci>
          <ci>khanary_topology.gml</ci>
          <ci>hypercube_Q3.gml</ci>
          <ci>hypercube_Q4.gml</ci>
        </list>
        <ci>gravity_field.cpp</ci>
        <ci>MicronautAttraction</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
GravityWellGeometry: topology GMLs define the geometry of gravity wells; FieldParamRecord GMLs
define field values inside wells at query time. The two roles must not be collapsed.

Gravity scoring law (src/micronaut/gravity_field.cpp):
  GravityScore(µ, Q) = established_nodes(µ) / distance²(Q, µ)
  established_nodes: count of gram/evidence nodes registered to µ — the well's mass.
  distance²: squared distance from query Q to µ's position in the product graph.

Topology GMLs supply BOTH inputs to this formula:
  unfold-graph.gml  → distance metric: Hamming distance between Q3 bit addresses (semantic distance),
                       C6 step count (phase distance). Adjacency edges define d=1 neighbors.
                       Combined distance: d²(Q,µ) uses the product-graph path length in Q_3 □ C_6.
  khanary_topology.gml → gravity center positions: x/y/z coordinates for each micronaut in Q3 space.
                       MicronautAttraction (vectors.mml): Φ_µ(Q) = Mass_µ · cos(Q, K_µ) · WCR,
                       where cos(Q, K_µ) is computed from these coordinate vectors.
  hypercube_Q3.gml  → fold edges (complement b→b̄, weight=1.0): cross-well shortcuts at Hamming
                       distance 3 that collapse the Q3 diameter from 3 to 2 (FQ3 is 4-regular).
  hypercube_Q4.gml  → Q4 allocation slot geometry: correct positions for MORPHISM-µ, FIXED-POINT-µ,
                       and Coordinator-counterpart. These are empty wells — geometry without mass.
                       Factory::propose_create() mints established_nodes into them; until then
                       GravityScore(slot, Q) = 0 / distance² = 0 for all Q.

FieldParamRecord GMLs supply field values INSIDE a well, not the well geometry:
  entropy_gradient_field.gml → entropy thresholds that modulate scoring once Q is in range.
  tensor_field.gml           → local metric curvature that warps distance near the well center.
  quantum_field_boundaries.gml → boundary conditions at the well perimeter (wave/refractive).
  euclidean_gradient_field.gml → potential gradient along the steepest approach path.
These parameters are cbuffer inputs to the scoring kernel; they do not define well positions
or the distance metric. Changing a curvature constant in tensor_field.gml does not move a well.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>FieldParamRecord</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>GML</mi>
      <mo>&#x2243;</mo>
      <mi>cbuffer</mi>
      <mo>&#x2295;</mo>
      <mi>topology_stub</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">FieldParamRecord</csymbol>
        <list>
          <ci>quantum_field_boundaries.gml</ci>
          <ci>tensor_field.gml</ci>
          <ci>entropy_gradient_field.gml</ci>
          <ci>euclidean_gradient_field.gml</ci>
        </list>
        <list>
          <ci>wave_number</ci>
          <ci>refractive</ci>
          <ci>amplitude_re_im</ci>
          <ci>g_metric_tensor</ci>
          <ci>riemann_curvature_scalar</ci>
          <ci>jacobian_determinant</ci>
          <ci>diffusion_beta_inv</ci>
          <ci>entropy_bound</ci>
          <ci>scalar_potential</ci>
          <ci>curl</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
FieldParamRecord: field GML files are typed parameter records, not topology descriptions.
FieldDag::load_gml() parses their node/edge attributes into FieldParamRecord entries and does
not overlay them into FieldDag adjacency. `field_param_records()` exposes the loaded values;
`find_field_param_record(field_kind,label,element_kind)` provides exact typed lookup. Parsing
and lookup establish availability, not an active runtime consumer. Current consumer status:

  quantum_field_boundaries.gml
    Role: wave/boundary parameter record for VECTOR-µ propagation.
    Constants: wave_number=2.1/1.4, frequency=0.75, amplitude_re/im, refractive index (3.4 for boundary reset),
               phase_shift (π/4, π/2), Kirchhoff source (divergence=+1.0) / sink (divergence=-1.0), Robin mixed.
    Status: parsed and available by exact label. NOT currently forwarded into
            dispatch_geodesic_propagator(); no boundary-to-runtime-node binding contract exists.

  tensor_field.gml
    Role: Riemannian metric tensor record for the bundle connection (TensorSubstrate binding layer).
    Constants: g_00=-0.8524, g_01=g_10=0.0125, g_11=1.1486 (non-Euclidean local metric),
               jacobian_w=1.0834, riemann_curvature_scalar=-0.412, tensor_rank_p=tensor_rank_q=1.
    Status: parsed and available by exact label. `VectorMuMicronaut::ExecuteProjection()` now
            accepts an explicit FieldParamRecord and observation, returning a typed bounded
            projection with provenance. It does NOT yet implement metric parallel transport,
            nor is it wired to a production request path.

  entropy_gradient_field.gml
    Role: Omega gate threshold record for ambiguity gating.
    Constants: entropy_bound=4.00, diffusion_beta_inv=0.25, entropy_spike threshold (3.67 = high-entropy example).
    Status: `diffusion_beta_inv` is forwarded to the geodesic propagator cbuffer (b0), with
            the function argument as fallback. The normalized routing Omega threshold remains
            the separate provisional constant 0.90; `entropy_bound`/`entropy_spike` are not
            currently wired into request-router admission.
    Note: node labels are example sentences illustrating low-entropy (0.15) vs high-entropy (3.82) inputs.

  euclidean_gradient_field.gml
    Role: conservative gradient field parameters for path-independent semantic progression.
    Constants: curl_x=curl_y=curl_z=0.0 (conservative — no holonomy), potential_delta=0.75,
               arc_length=2.8284 (√8 diagonal), scalar_potential range [0.20, 0.95].
    Status: parsed and available by exact label. Conservative edge records are marked only
            when all three curl components are present and within tolerance. The propagator
            does NOT yet consume this gradient; mapping this sample path onto runtime graph
            edges is not defined.

  metric_graph.gml
    Role: METRIC-µ provider topology (18 nodes). Distinct from the above — this IS a topology graph,
    but its authority boundary is different: FoldGraph_B is authoritative; METRIC-µ aggregates
    providers (VECTOR-µ, SDR, GRAPH, SCX_keybook) and never commits topology B (edge 109).
    Cross-track metric requires explicit bridge admission (Bridge_JOKE_ELIZA pattern).

  sample.gml — GML parser test fixture (3 nodes, 3 directed edges in a cycle). No field or semantic role.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>GMLLoadLaw</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>load_gml</mi>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>TensorSubstrate</mi>
      <mo>&#x2260;</mo>
      <mi>MicronautEntry</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:gml-topology:v1">GMLLoadAuthorityLaw</csymbol>
        <ci>FieldDag::load_gml</ci>
        <ci>TensorSubstrate</ci>
        <ci>MicronautEntry</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
GMLLoadAuthorityLaw: FieldDag::load_gml() creates TensorSubstrate descriptors, not MicronautEntry objects.
  For each unique provider_id found in GML nodes, one TensorSubstrate entry is created (residency=HOST_RAM).
  After dispatch_geodesic_propagator() runs, substrates are promoted to GPU_VRAM_D3D11.
  A TensorSubstrate with a geometry-source provider_id (e.g. "brain4-expert-34") is projection-only.
  It MUST NOT be promoted to a MicronautEntry in the registry.
  Only TrackLoader (JSON track files) and Factory::propose_create() may create MicronautEntry objects.
  GML topology is geometry and legal-adjacency input; the semantic interpretation is XCFE/phase authority.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
GMLTopology contract invariants:
1. G_runtime = Q_n □ C_6 with n=3 (unfold-graph.gml): 48 vertices, deg(v)=5, legal transitions are d_H=1.
2. Semantic bit schema (b0/b1/b2) is the address space; tracks occupy named positions, not IDs.
3. Q4 b3=1 positions are ALLOCATION slots; an unoccupied slot is valid — Factory may mint into it.
4. CCC(n) graphs are 3-regular interconnection substrates; XOR edges = cross-cluster bit-flip routing.
5. Field GML files (quantum/tensor/entropy/euclidean) are typed parameter records, not topology graphs.
   Only entropy diffusion beta is currently forwarded to the geodesic propagator. VectorMu accepts an
   explicit record for bounded numeric projection, but there is no production request-path call and this
   is not metric parallel transport. Quantum boundary values, Euclidean gradient values, and Omega
   entropy thresholds are parsed/looked up only. No field record may commit FoldGraph topology B.
   metric_graph.gml is a topology graph but also carries no B-commit authority.
6. FieldDag::load_gml() → TensorSubstrate only; MicronautEntry creation is TrackLoader/Factory exclusive.
7. sample.gml is a parser test fixture; it carries no semantic or topology authority.
8. GravityWellGeometry: topology GMLs (unfold-graph, khanary_topology, hypercube_Q3/Q4) define well
   positions and the distance metric for GravityScore(µ,Q) = established_nodes/distance².
   FieldParamRecord GMLs define field values inside wells (cbuffer inputs to scoring kernels).
   Q4 allocation slots are empty wells (mass=0) until Factory::propose_create() mints into them.
  </annotation>
</math>
